codex
One implementation issue surfaced in the repository’s static checks: the original escalation only lengthened the bit witness. I’m adding a genuine fixed-witness-length hardness axis—the public convolution may be the inverse of a second power of the same sparse cyclic operator—before allowing `n` to grow again. The shipping case remains exactly the already-hardened `n=47`, power-one instance, so its oracle evidence remains applicable.
